WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.950
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.380
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.600
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:41.200
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.920
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.660
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.300
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.550
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:16.100
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.080
Labophase

12
00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.650
Stussy...

13
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.770
It’s me...

14
00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:48.900
Edison!

15
00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.820
Deactivate da barrier and run...

16
00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.070
Wha?

17
00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:57.410
I can’t! I don’t want anything to happen
to the Straw Hats before they leave.

18
00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:02.040
Honestly... Da barrier ain’t doin’ us
 no good no more.

19
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.260
Not against these folks
who can just get past it anyway...

20
00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:22.770
Ah’ve already done my best
to ensure da Straw Hats’ escape.

21
00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:27.980
Dey’ll manage da rest, somehow.

22
00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.570
Good to know.

23
00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:33.440
If they don’t make it,

24
00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.200
Stella would hate me.

25
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.370
Nah, he wouldn’t.

26
00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.660
But ya gotta get out now!

27
00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.370
But...

28
00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.420
I’m stumped...

29
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.630
Now without Stella,

30
00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:52.420
I don’t know who to live for...

31
00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:56.970
anymore...

32
00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.350
Jinbe, why aren’t you here yet?!

33
00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.020
Sorry! We’re almost there.

34
00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:09.110
You don’t gotta apologize, Jinbe.
We’re running as fast as we can.

35
00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:12.360
You say something, Zoro?!
I’m kicking your ass later!

36
00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:23.830
Hurry up! Ships are starting to converge
 off the northeast coast.

37
00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:27.540
I don’t wanna be under attack
as soon as we land on the water!

38
00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.040
Let’s move, then!

39
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.260
That old fart can cut through anything!

40
00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.850
Don’t let him use his sword!

41
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.310
Concassé!

42
00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.490
Go to hell, geezer!

43
00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:16.840
Wha—

44
00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.430
Life-form detected...

45
00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.520
Bonney!

46
00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:31.850
Bonney!

47
00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:38.490
Whoa!

48
00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:41.320
My future form
doesn’t last for long...

49
00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.870
C’mon, now...
Don’t push yourself too far!

50
00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.450
We can’t drop our guard!

51
00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.790
Stinkin’ old guy...!

52
00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.000
Nuh?!

53
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.080
Where’s he going?!

54
00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.340
The Void Century...

55
00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:02.640
came to an end
 with Joyboy’s defeat.

56
00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:08.430
How long do you intend to
prattle on, Vegapunk?!

57
00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:12.900
It ended, leaving behind...

58
00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:16.110
the incalculable,
 irreparable ravages of war...

59
00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:21.820
Obnoxious life-form!

60
00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:04.700
Our world is made up of
 a series of islands.

61
00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.620
Crossing the seas poses difficulties,

62
00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.830
so many people spend their entire lives
 without exploring foreign cultures.

63
00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:14.250
Why is he stating the obvious now?

64
00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.080
The seas are simply too dangerous.

65
00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.500
But this common
 understanding of the world...

66
00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:22.510
does not necessarily apply to
 the world of a thousand years ago.

67
00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:26.930
A cataclysm during the Void Century...

68
00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.760
caused the world...

69
00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.810
to sink into the sea once before.

70
00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:42.360
We’re now living atop scattered pieces of
 what were once continents.

71
00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:48.070
The world sank into the sea?!
Atop scattered pieces of continents?!

72
00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:53.450
The world from a millennium ago
 is now ruined, lying at the bottom of the sea.

73
00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.710
It is believed that, in ancient times,

74
00:06:55.710 --> 00:07:00.000
there were several continents
 in the world of which we have no record.

75
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.420
This is quite a revelation.

76
00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.470
Hey! Where are you going, Nojiko?

77
00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.090
The world is in danger...

78
00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:08.680
Fill me in later.

79
00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:11.560
I’m going to check on
the tangerine field.

80
00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.680
Nojiko!

81
00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:19.610
If the world hadn’t changed at all
 from the past,

82
00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:25.030
erasing all traces of a century of history
 from the records would be impossible.

83
00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:27.740
It makes much more sense,
 however, if...

84
00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:31.620
you consider that, in a mere hundred years,
 the sea level rose by the astonishing amount of...

85
00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.790
two hundred meters!

86
00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:38.250
What?! T-T-Two hundred meters?!

87
00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:41.920
Even this massive warship
is only sixty meters long!

88
00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:44.130
No wonder the whole world vanished...

89
00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.420
Dammit, men!
Don’t just stand around listening to the speech!

90
00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.260
We’ve got Cipher Pol and Seraphim
falling out of the sky!

91
00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:51.370
Rescue them, now!

92
00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.830
Mock
 Town,
Town of
Ridicule

93
00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:56.060
You hearin’ this guy?!
He just keeps comin’ up with this stuff!

94
00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:58.270
The old fart’s a total riot!

95
00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:00.980
How’s that even possible?!

96
00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.430
Sakura
Kingdom

(Chopper's
homeland)

97
00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.490
How does such a thing happen?

98
00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:12.030
This world of ours
still has so much wonder in it!

99
00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:15.580
That mountain is just about
two hundred meters high.

100
00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.710
That’s how high the sea level rose?

101
00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:21.690
Sounds like hell...
How many people would die from that?!

102
00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:24.160
Water
Seven,
City of
Water

103
00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:28.170
Why did the sea level rise
 during that century, then?

104
00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:33.260
It stands to reason that the cause
would be an unexpected natural calamity.

105
00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:38.060
But I’m certain
the disaster was man-made.

106
00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:42.900
There’s just no freakin’ way!

107
00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:50.070
Were such a cataclysm
caused by natural forces,

108
00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:53.320
the initial disaster would have spanned
several centuries...

109
00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:57.040
and inflicted slow
but continuous damage upon the world.

110
00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:00.080
That can’t be true! I don’t buy it!

111
00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:08.420
But by any measurement — climatology, geology,
 environmental and atmospheric science —

112
00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:12.130
this dramatic shift could not have happened
 within a single century!

113
00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.100
Therefore, the cause
must be something else.

114
00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:19.140
When I detected the rise
 in worldwide sea levels the other day,

115
00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:22.020
I had my answer.

116
00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:30.690
I knew the cause,
 and confirmed its existence!

117
00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:37.160
The Ancient Weapons that sank the world
 eight hundred years ago still exist,

118
00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.660
and await the day
 they are once again activated!

119
00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:52.590
That is to say, the great war
 that erupted during the Void Century...

120
00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:59.640
has not yet ended!

121
00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:06.730
You gotta be kidding!

122
00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:10.480
The weapons that sank the world
are still out there somewhere?!

123
00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:13.280
The war from eight hundred years ago
is still ongoing?

124
00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:14.030
Where?!

125
00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:16.410
No one from back then is still alive!

126
00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:20.700
How can a war be ongoing
if nobody knows about it, Vegapunk?!

127
00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.460
I...

128
00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:35.050
must apologize deeply.

129
00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:37.760
But I need you to know this!

130
00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:49.440
I wanted to create a source of power
 essential for the future growth of this world’s industries.

131
00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:52.320
It is still incomplete, however!

132
00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:59.320
The Mother Flame, the culmination of my research,
has just reached the stage of practical use!

133
00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:04.960
It is a power source that will surely enrich
the lives of people in all countries someday!

134
00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:07.790
However...

135
00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:11.500
a fragment of that flame
 was stolen one day.

136
00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:17.180
It’s all my fault.

137
00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.680
Cipher Pol agents
are at the center of the island?!

138
00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:24.890
It’s impossible to rescue them!
The whole island’s covered in flames!

139
00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:33.570
It’s shaking so much!
 What happened, Edison?!

140
00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:36.110
Scared me, too.

141
00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.780
It’s a mess...

142
00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:43.040
Da Labophase’s underground lab and
Cipher Pol agents came fallin’ to da ground.

143
00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.370
We’ve been beat...

144
00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:49.120
Ah can’t send no more Island Clouds
for da Straw Hats.

145
00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:52.090
What do you mean they fell?!

146
00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:56.670
One of those crazy Five Elders
is headin’ yer way!

147
00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:02.600
You gotta run, Stussy. Please.

148
00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:11.310
Can I release Kaku, then, Edison?

149
00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.150
Wha?

150
00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:17.030
He and Lucci may
face punishment for this.

151
00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:19.740
I won’t let him chase
after the Straw Hats,

152
00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:23.450
but I know full well
what he will do next.

153
00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:28.790
Ah understand, Stussy.

154
00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:32.170
Ah’m sorry Ah put ya through all that...

155
00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:34.420
Y’all were friends, yeah?

156
00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.380
Ah feel bad for makin’ ya betray them.

157
00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:43.140
But still, ya helped us.

158
00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:45.040
Ya really care about both them and us.

159
00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:51.020
Feelin’ conflicted proves that
yer human, Stussy.

160
00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.900
Live your life however you want
 from now on,

161
00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.110
but promise me yer gonna survive!

162
00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:00.200
I will!

163
00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:07.330
Roughly two weeks
 after the flame was stolen,

164
00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:11.290
we received word of a violent flash in
 the skies over Lulusia...

165
00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:12.670
Lulusia...

166
00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:17.130
followed by intel that the kingdom
had vanished without a trace.

167
00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:19.710
Somebody destroyed Lulusia?!

168
00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:24.430
And what’s more, after that, we observed
 the signs of an imminent worldwide quake.

169
00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:27.720
As a scientist,
 and with pride in my development...

170
00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:30.390
That was caused by one of
the Ancient Weapons?!

171
00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:35.000
Kingdom of
Prodence

172
00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:35.020
Nothing but the Mother Flame could have
created such an immense amount of energy!

173
00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:37.480
The Kingdom of Lulusia is gone?!

174
00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.610
We haven’t received such information.

175
00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:41.900
Verify it, immediately!

176
00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:42.360
Yes, sire!

177
00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:44.320
The flame that I created...

178
00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.530
was used to activate
 an Ancient Weapon!

179
00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.960
I have absolutely no idea
 who carried it out,

180
00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.380
but the results speak for themselves!

181
00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:00.670
I was complicit
 in the taking of numerous lives.

182
00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:04.130
As such, I feel personally responsible!
I am truly sorry!

183
00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:08.220
The artificial catastrophe
that once sank this world...

184
00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:10.930
has been shown to be possible.

185
00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:13.290
Vegapunk! It’s not your fault!

186
00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.250
Flower Capital












Land of Wano

187
00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:15.270
What?!

188
00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:16.810
Then Pluton is—

189
00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:20.730
Momonosuke-sama!

190
00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.190
I implore you to mind your words!

191
00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:25.890
Understood. My apologies.

192
00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:27.900
Buggy
District

Emptee Bluffs
Island

New World

193
00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:30.370
In the past,
 there were three Ancient Weapons,

194
00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:34.710
and Joyboy sought to pass them on
 to future generations.

195
00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:39.250
Why did he do that?
 Did he want the world to sink more?

196
00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:42.210
Who is evil and who is good?!

197
00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:45.430
There will be a time
 when all the answers come clear!

198
00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:50.310
You’re going to choke.

199
00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:55.350
I told you, you silly man...

200
00:14:55.350 --> 00:15:01.320
And I warn you, that moment will happen
when we reach the very precipice of the world’s drowning!

201
00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:09.240
The Void Century
still remains full of unknowns.

202
00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:12.740
But, there are people
who have learned the whole truth!

203
00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:17.040
You really are going to
spill the beans, huh,

204
00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.710
Vegapunk?!

205
00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:21.540
The Pirate King’s crew.

206
00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.510
What?!

207
00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:26.130
Pirates?!

208
00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:27.090
Why?!

209
00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:36.690
Why are the secrets of the world
in the hands of pirates?!

210
00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:38.140
It’s too dangerous!

211
00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:43.360
Huh?

212
00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:46.110
Wait a minute.

213
00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:48.360
That’s strange.

214
00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:52.910
Stella, how’d you know
I stole the Mother Flame?

215
00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:56.120
The synchronization was turned off.
You wouldn’ta found me out!

216
00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:59.670
I know you as a terrible liar and actor!

217
00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:01.840
At that moment...

218
00:16:03.590 --> 00:16:05.090
York!

219
00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:08.260
Is this all your doing?!

220
00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:11.470
You were truly shocked!

221
00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:15.930
You received word of Lulusia
and observed the data?

222
00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.270
What does that mean?

223
00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:18.730
When?

224
00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:20.810
The timeline doesn’t add up!

225
00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:24.770
You knew what the Government would do?

226
00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.740
But if that’s the case,
then I had it all wrong!

227
00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:31.490
He wouldn’t do something half-assed
like just hiding the Transmission Transponder Snail!

228
00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:46.380
Five Elders!

229
00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:49.550
I know where
 the Transmission Transponder Snail is!

230
00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:53.550
Are you certain?

231
00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:55.260
I am!

232
00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:58.020
I’s a Vegapunk, too!

233
00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:01.690
The Transmission Transponder Snail
is in the Fabriophase,

234
00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:05.520
protected by the Iron Giant!

235
00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:19.040
No good! Nothing’s working!

236
00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:40.600
Why did those who learned the truth
 fade away without telling anyone anything?

237
00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:43.230
Why didn’t they act on it?

238
00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:49.650
Ray-san.

239
00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:53.070
You’re drinking too much.

240
00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:59.040
Well, I’m just another old man now.

241
00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:06.250
It’s not like you to be this wiped out...

242
00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:10.590
And you’re telling them too much, Vegapunk...

243
00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:14.760
Us old folk should keep our secrets...

244
00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:18.680
and not ruin it for the young’uns,
you damn fool...

245
00:18:24.190 --> 00:18:26.650
Right, Roger?

246
00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:29.820
Let the kids have their fun...

247
00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:43.610
